A graphics application uses a class to represent screen coordinates. What will be displayed when the following code runs?

class Coordinate(object):
    def __init__(self, x, y):
        self.x = x
        self.y = y
    def display(self):
        print(f"Position: ({self.x}, {self.y})")
cursor = Coordinate(15, 30)
cursor.display()

